From 3f7268bb766a47fe66552865843205584b90dd84 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mecattaf <thomas@mecattaf.dev>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 16:48:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] [ROCm] Defer the inner CausalLM build_tables on the
 multimodal PLE path

TP=2 first light on the FULL multimodal checkpoint died deterministically
on both ranks, ~40 s into serve, at 0/131 safetensors FILES:

  RuntimeError: PLE mmap: layer 1 weight_scale was never loaded from the
  checkpoint's streamed weights

raised from _attach_table via build_tables. The TP=1 PLE-only proxy
checkpoint never exercised this path, so it shipped green.

The tensor is not missing. In this checkpoint's
model.safetensors.index.json (152089 tensors) the one PLE layer's
model.language_model.layers.1.ple.ple_embedding.ngram_embedding.weight_scale
lives in model-00005-of-00131.safetensors, so at 0/131 it simply has not
streamed yet. The raise is correct; the CALL is early.

Mechanism: AutoWeightsLoader dispatches a child module's load_weights
once per CONTIGUOUS RUN of that child's prefix in the weight stream, not
once at the end. On Qwen4ExpForConditionalGeneration the visual.* tensors
interleave with model.language_model.*, so the inner
Qwen4ExpForCausalLM.load_weights returns -- and calls build_tables --
while the language-model stream is still in progress. The wrapper's own
post-stream build_tables call at the end of
Qwen4ExpForConditionalGeneration.load_weights is the one that is
genuinely after the whole checkpoint.

Fix, three lines, no change to the fail-closed raise:

  Qwen4ExpForCausalLM.__init__      self._ple_build_tables_deferred = False
  Qwen4ExpForCausalLM.load_weights  gate build_tables on `not deferred`
  Qwen4ExpForConditionalGeneration.__init__
                                    set the flag True on the inner
                                    language_model it just constructed

Standalone Qwen4ExpForCausalLM is untouched: the flag stays False and the
single post-stream call still fires (the existing "exactly once" test
asserts it). --load-format dummy never runs load_weights at all. Every
remaining call site now runs strictly after the complete stream, so the
weight_scale raise keeps its full fail-closed strength -- it just can no
longer fire on a load that was always going to succeed.

nvidia/model.py is byte-mirrored from amd/model.py, preserving the
patch-0010 parity invariant (cmp confirms identical).

build_tables' docstring is amended, not its code: the paragraph asserting
that the inner CausalLM call reaches build_tables mid-load is now false,
and the repeat-call cost paragraph is retargeted at reload_weights, which
is the only remaining repeat caller.

tests/models/qwen4_exp/test_ple_mmap.py: the existing stub-based
test_model_load_weights_calls_build_tables_exactly_once_when_enabled
drives load_weights with a SimpleNamespace `self` and needs the new
attribute; adds test_causal_lm_load_weights_skips_build_tables_when_
deferred pinning that flag=True + VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1 never calls
build_tables.

Verified in flashnext:dev on gfx1151 with the edited tree bind-mounted
over /opt/vllm: amd and nvidia model modules import clean in separate
processes, and all five PLE suites pass one-file-per-process --
test_ple_mmap.py 83 (82 + the new pin), test_ple_mmap_amd.py 15,
test_ple_mmap_host_registration.py 30, test_ple.py 11,
test_weight_loading.py 30; 169 total, zero failures.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015yaArXNiA4ThqRxNrTnEMC
